today I'm going to share my best career  advice for young people and its really  different than what you might hear from  others hi I'm Evan Carmichael  I believe in entrepreneurs and I really  got a great question for one of my  newsletter subscribers love you guys  Sneha I hope I pronounced that properly  who wrote in to say hey Evan I hope you  do read this mail and really hope you  can advise me Here I am let's go till  the time I graduated I just fixated on  being someone with a capital S it's  quite sad perhaps that I did not know  exactly what I wanted to be in life at  that time being just someone and  something big seemed important I  graduated in 2014 and got hired for  Deloitte the past five months I enjoyed  like I never had from being extremely  introverted I changed to being some  social I got confidence and also my job  demands networking it has all worked out  perfectly well until now I realized that  there is no more to life than one little  accomplishment so obvious that is I know  where I want to go I will admit I'm not  an entrepreneur type but I do not want  to expand my skill set I believe it can  be a good team leader not now but  someday there's a lot I have to work on  and I'm ready for those challenges I was  hoping you could tell me a few essential  things that I should not miss while  climbing up the ladder  how should I get the best out of my  company I'm not an extrovert so what  ways are there of networking are they  always about socializing with people on  personal level how do I learn most  effectively and improve my value in the  company I know there's a lot of  questions but please help me out I  really need your advice thanks a lot for  taking the timeliness email it means a  lot to me thanks and regards snow this  is a fantastic question and I think one  that a lot of young people face I think  every young person faces at some point  trying to figure out what you want to do  with your life and I think with every  big decision and I've talked about this  on the channel every big decision you  make is with the heart and not the head  right stop thinking so much and start  acting more now that's not saying be  totally reckless and go crazy you know  it's good to have a little bit of a gut  check there but too many people  overthink and as a result what happens  is you stay within the box that's what's  happening right corporate America is a  box and and I'm not saying you have to  be an entrepreneur it's totally cool you  don't be an entrepreneur something for  everybody but be an entrepreneur with  in the corporation what happens to so  many people is they get on a career path  and it's so well-defined for them right  you start off here you go here you go  here you go here you go here you'll be  here and gradually as you move up most  people become more and more and more and  more miserable right most people hate  their jobs and they're living for the  weekends and living for the the evenings  and they don't like their life right  they feel like they haven't become that  somebody with a capital S so the way to  do it and have success is to follow your  heart within the organization and  that'll mean stepping outside the box  that the corporation has defined for you  so you know your manager wants you to do  these five things well you know maybe  your colleague is working on a project  that really excites you go help them as  well maybe you've seen initiative that  you could be a leader on and help bring  to the company go work on that as well  and try to bring it don't ask for as  much permission still do the job you  know you're not getting in trouble from  your manager but look for other ways to  expand yourself and pull your heart and  passion to something even if it's  totally outside your current domain  because what most people follow is that  path of linear growth right you're  slowly moving up the ladder  we're really if you want to have massive  success and you want to be tremendously  happy in your life as well it's going to  look a lot Messier right if you don't  know where you want to go you don't know  quite where the top is going to be for  you it'll be really messy you're gonna  jump from here to here to here to here  to here to here to here and slowly  you're you'll move up you might move  down a little bit and then you'll take a  huge leap forward and that's normal  right that's fine that's okay but it's  not the safe thing that most people do  most people get locked in one thing and  that's where they are for the rest of  their careers look at something like  networking okay you hate networking I  ain't networking I'm not great at  networking I'm an introvert you may not  believe from the videos you know I can  get excited and get vocal I can yell the  videos but I am I am by nature and  introvert I don't talk to people on the  airplane I'm not talking to the guy next  to me I hate networking events with a  passion I don't know what to say I'm  clumsy I don't want to go up to summer's  day hi I'm Evan who are you what are you  all about some people are great at that  some people are like for the party  they really stand out they're amazing  That's not me it sounds like it's not  you so for you to think that you have to  have a networking skill to be effective  in your company that's living inside the  box and you're always going to be  restricted by that because it's not who  you are by nature so many people focus  on their weaknesses and what they're not  great at and trying to improve it  instead of focusing on what you're  really great at and being one of the  best in the world at that instead of  being a mediocre networker and slowly  moving your way up you could double down  on your strengths and do something that  you are so unbelievably amazing that to  build an amazing future for yourself so  for me again I hate networking the way I  flipped it was I'll only go to events  where I'm speaking right I've built  myself up as an authority in my industry  and now I'm speaking at events instead  of attending as a networker the only  other events I'll go to is where I'm  genuinely interested in learning from  the speaker or from the people who are  going to be there in which case I have  something in common right I'm not going  there just to hobnob with some of the  people and try to get to know them I'm  going there to actually better myself  and learn which gives me something to  potentially talk to people about so flip  it if you are not going to be the master  networker it's not you're in your DNA  it's not part of your personality it's  not a skill that's worth for you to  really double down on and maximize  because that's not who you are then  think about how can you flip that how  can you be the speaker at the next event  or how can you set up and be the creator  of the events and have people come to  you right create a system where people  want to come and talk to you instead of  you having to go out and talk to them  and that's just one example there are  probably countless of examples and  examples of examples of how you think  that this is the only way to succeed  because that's how corporate America  tells me to succeed and that's how  everybody in the company has succeeded  so far where you'll have a lot more  success if you are able to think outside  of that box break free  don't let them define who you are  because if you are living somebody  else's expectations of who you're going  to be you're never going to be the best  version of yourself  you're never going to come  the success that you can you're never  going to have the impact that you're you  would be able to have you're never going  to be that somebody with a capital S  because you're living somebody else's  expectations on you to be a great team  leader to be a great networker to be a  great fill in the blank and instead you  need to live your own version of your  life better on your strengths be the  best person in the world at what you do  and that brings tremendous value to your  company and gives you the best chance at  not only success but also happiness and  impact which I think are pretty  important so thank you very question and  continue to believe for those you're  watching I'd love to know what you think  I want a little bit of a rant and a tie  rate there let me know what you think  about how to have success in corporate  America leave a comment underneath I'd  love to see what you have to think and  of course if you like this video and you  want to see more don't forget to  subscribe to the channel and the  newsletter thank you so much for  watching I'll see you soon

